    "content": "Yes, clashes with only Reverse mode enabled should either have an effectively empty statement or display a warning upfront.\n\nGoal\n* Please add at the beginning:\n<<This clash is in Reverse mode only.>>\n\nStub generator\n* Please change \"n\" to \"A\".\n\n* Please change \"N\" to \"B\".\n\n* Please add a write statement.\n\nCases\n* Validator 1: Please change the input so that [[A]] < [[B]] and the GCD is 1, similar to Test 1.\n\n* Please add Test 5 and Validator 5 where [[A]] is a multiple of [[B]] and [[A]] ≠ [[B]].\n\n* Please add Test 6 and Validator 6 where [[B]] is a multiple of [[A]] and [[A]] ≠ [[B]].\n\n* Please add Test 7 and Validator 7 where [[A]] = [[B]].\n\n* Please add Test 8 and Validator 8 where [[A]] > [[B]] and the GCD is 1.\n\n* Please add Test 9 and Validator 9 where [[A]] > [[B]] and the GCD is greater than 1.\n\n* Please add Test 10 and Validator 10 where [[A]] > [[B]] and the GCD is greater than 19.\n\nThanks.",
